From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:26:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] contacts: sync names from the primary and resolve unknown
 senders

Address-book names only reach a linked device through the contact sync,
which was requested only when the device was linked. Contacts added or
renamed since then stayed nameless. Request the sync on every login,
bounded by a 20 s timeout, and retry it in the background after 45, 90,
180 and 360 s so a slow or sleeping primary does not lose the whole
contact list until the next login.

Contacts that are not in the address book (only messaged) get their
name from a profile fetch. Do that in a spawned task on a cloned
manager, at most once per UUID per session, using the profile key from
the contact's own message when available. The receive loop never waits
on it, so a hung profile request cannot stall message delivery.

When no name is known, alias the buddy to its phone number rather than
the raw UUID.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/rust/src/contacts.rs | 150 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/rust/src/core.rs     |  33 ++++++++-
 src/rust/src/receive.rs  |  42 ++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

